refactor(l10n): data-driven language catalog backing AppLocale

Replace the per-language switch statements in AppLocale with a single
data-driven LanguageCatalog of LanguageDescriptor entries that own each
language's code, native display name, ordered fallback chain, and a
bundled-vs-downloadable availability flag.

- Add LanguageDescriptor (pure value type) and LanguageCatalog (single
  source of truth, ordered to match AppLocale.allCases) in Hanahuac/L10n/.
- Back AppLocale.displayName, fallbackChain, fallsBackThroughSpanish, and
  the new isBundledBaseLanguage accessor with catalog lookups.
- Resolve AppLocale.matching simple per-code cases (en, fr, de, ko) via the
  catalog; keep the es-* and Nahuatl ISO-639-3 special cases.
- Derive L10n.bundleCandidates from the descriptor fallback chain, keeping
  output byte-identical (incl. the historical ["en","en"] for the base).
- Add LanguageCatalogTests; existing AppLocaleTests and LanguageManagerTests
  pass unchanged.

Pure internal re-architecture, no user-visible behavior change.

